 "notes": "NASDUCK-SERF (K/3He SERF comagnetometer). Headline result: first terrestrial ALP-proton DM bound (abstract emphasizes protons). Traced the grey geometric-mean line of the ALP-proton panel (protons.pdf, Fig 2 right), which the paper presents as the representative limit (median-in-bin of the vector polyline idx 83). Paper plots g_aPP in GeV^-1 for the gradient/derivative coupling H=g_aPP grad(a).spin; converted to canonical dimensionless g_ap via the 2m_N rule g_ap=2 m_p g_aPP (m_p=0.9383 GeV). Native mean line ranges ~5.4e-6 to ~3e-5 GeV^-1, consistent with abstract statement about partially closing 5e-6 to 2e-5 GeV^-1. Axes calibrated from tick labels (x:103.3px/decade, m 1.4e-12 to 2e-10 eV; y:35.5px/decade). Paper also bounds ALP-neutron (g_aNN, neutrons.pdf) but presents protons as the main novel result. dm_density not stated in main text/e-print; 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed per NASDUCK convention. Data also tabulated as .pkl in external GitHub (Ref 57), not used. CL=95%.",
